WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
The world's oldest dated
printed book is a Buddhist text:

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.720
the Diamond Sutra, printed in 868.

3
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:12.680
It belongs to a family of Mahayana
texts called the Perfection of Wisdom.

4
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:18.910
Its tiny sister, the Heart Sutra, is chanted
every day by many Mahayana Buddhists.

5
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.820
And it says something startling:
no suffering, no path.

6
00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:27.510
So why would Buddhists
chant those words every day?

7
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:32.000
In this mission, you'll follow how the
idea that everything changes grew into

8
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.190
the teaching of emptiness.

9
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.370
Then you'll read the
sutra's most famous lines:

10
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:41.310
form is emptiness, emptiness is form.

11
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:46.680
Your mission: explain why Buddhists would
chant a text that says no suffering,

12
00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:47.650
no path.
